=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  play users/debian13 ------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: users/debian13$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13. As the VM: george, uid$
# 1000, no password (!), in sudo and adm, two keys, NOPASSWD by$
# cloud-init's 90-cloud-init-users; alice, uid 1001, a password,$
# in sudo, no key. hardn runs through george's sudo.$
$
# User Management ##############################################$
$
  [+] User                 Configured non-root, sudo$
$
  george -------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Sudo                 Enabled, No password to ask for$
   -  Granted by           /etc/sudoers.d/90-cloud-init-users$
   -  SSH Keys             2 keys$
   -  Password             None$
$
  alice --------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Sudo                 Enabled$
   -  Granted by           group sudo$
  [ ] SSH Keys             None$
   -  Password             Set$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Manage User          Configure sudo, SSH keys$
   2) Create User          Configure a new user$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter your choice [0-2 or q]: 1$
$
# Manage User ##################################################$
$
  Select a user$
$
   1) george$
   2) alice$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter your choice [0-2 or q]: 1$
$
# Manage User ##################################################$
$
  Managing: [george]$
$
  User Configuration -------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Sudo                 Enabled, No password to ask for$
   -  Granted by           /etc/sudoers.d/90-cloud-init-users$
   -  SSH Keys             2 keys$
   -  Password             None$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Remove admin rights  Take them away$
   2) Ask for password     For admin rights$
   3) SSH Keys             Add or remove SSH keys$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter your choice [0-3 or q]: 1$
$
# Warning$
# george is an admin through /etc/sudoers.d/90-cloud-init-users,$
# which hardn didn't write, so hardn can't remove it. Change it$
# there.$
$
# Manage User ##################################################$
$
  Managing: [george]$
$
  User Configuration -------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Sudo                 Enabled, No password to ask for$
   -  Granted by           /etc/sudoers.d/90-cloud-init-users$
   -  SSH Keys             2 keys$
   -  Password             None$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Remove admin rights  Take them away$
   2) Ask for password     For admin rights$
   3) SSH Keys             Add or remove SSH keys$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter your choice [0-3 or q]: 0$
$
# Manage User ##################################################$
$
  Select a user$
$
   1) george$
   2) alice$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter your choice [0-2 or q]: 0$
$
# User Management ##############################################$
$
  [+] User                 Configured non-root, sudo$
$
  george -------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Sudo                 Enabled, No password to ask for$
   -  Granted by           /etc/sudoers.d/90-cloud-init-users$
   -  SSH Keys             2 keys$
   -  Password             None$
$
  alice --------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Sudo                 Enabled$
   -  Granted by           group sudo$
  [ ] SSH Keys             None$
   -  Password             Set$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Manage User          Configure sudo, SSH keys$
   2) Create User          Configure a new user$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter your choice [0-2 or q]: 0$
$
  simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
